{"type": "thinking", "text": "\"1.2.3\" leaves Save disabled. Good validation.\n\nTest \"150abc\": type. Clear first... type_text appends? Earlier type_text with element seemed to clear partially weirdly. Here after typing 1.2.3, typing more appends? Let's just test \"150abc\" by selecting all and typing. That's laborious. Alternative: use keyboard, since type_text inserted the whole string. Hmm.\n\nLet me instead use adb-like approach: press DEL 5 times then type. Actually I can use press_key DEL multiple times. It's fine.\n\nActually let's not over-test the parser. The main hint says \"single number parser for every input\" — likely a bug where one field uses a different parser. In this test result editor, both Estradiol and Testosterone accepted \"150,5\" and \"45,5\" and saved as 150.5/45.5. Consistent.\n\nBut wait — maybe the bug is that one input parses \"1,5\" as 15 (thousands separator) while another parses as 1.5. We tested both with comma decimals and both became decimal. Good.\n\nWhat about a value like \"1,234\"? If parser treats comma as decimal → 1.234; if as grouping → 1234. Both fields? Could differ. But hard to know expected.\n\nAnother candidate: body weight editor parsed \"70,5\" fine.\n\nHmm, \"Settings measurement editor\" — maybe it's about \"Target range\" editor with min/max. Target range row was disabled because... It said clickable,disabled. Maybe it requires something. Hmm.\n\nCould there be a \"measurement editor\" in Settings under \"Widgets\"? Unlikely.\n\nWait, maybe I mis-assume. The changed item may refer to the Settings screen's \"Body weight\" measurement editor. It has a single input though. \"for every input\" might mean across different measurement editors (weight, etc.). Hmm.\n\nLet me test other things in Settings: \"First day of week\" and \"Hide reference ranges\" toggles, persistence. But the specific changed area is what to focus on. However task says sweep Settings generally.\n\nLet's continue: cancel this edit to avoid changing data. Cancel button."}
