{"type": "thinking", "text": "Preview now: Today 7:00 AM, Nov 16 Mon 7:00 AM, Nov 28 Sat 7:00 AM. Hmm — with \"repeat every 2 weeks\" and days Sat + Mon, expected: Sat Nov 14 (start), Mon Nov 16? Wait start date Nov 14 Sat. Repeat every 2 weeks on Sat & Mon. Anchor week starts... Nov 14 (week of Nov 9-15). Days Sat+Mon: also Mon Nov 9 (past) so next is Mon Nov 16 (in week Nov 16-22?) Hmm, if repeat every 2 weeks, week 2 would be Nov 16-22 (week index counting from start week?). Actually interval 2 weeks from Nov 14: week of Nov 9, then week of Nov 23. Mon Nov 16 is in week of Nov 16, which is 1 week after start week — not a repeated week. So preview showing Nov 16 Mon might be wrong? Hmm, depends on semantics: weekly recurrence with interval 2 may anchor to the start date's week, and days Mon/Sat. Start Sat Nov 14. Then next occurrences: Sat Nov 14 (today), Mon Nov 23 (2 weeks later? no...). Hmm.\n\nLet's think: \"every 2 weeks on Mon and Sat\" starting Sat Nov 14. Common calendar semantics: recurring event every 2 weeks, the selected week is the week containing the start date (Nov 9–15). Days: Sat Nov 14 (today), Mon Nov 9 (past, so skip). Next occurrence week: Nov 23–29: Mon Nov 23, Sat Nov 28. So the next after today should be Mon Nov 23, not Nov 16. So preview \"Nov 16 Mon\" is likely wrong! Because it includes Monday of the intervening week. Wait, unless the recurrence treats \"every 2 weeks\" as based on each selected weekday's own start: Monday Nov 16 would be 2 weeks after... no, Monday Nov 9 (past). Hmm.\n\nHmm, wait. Another interpretation: For a weekly schedule with interval N, weeks are counted from the start date week. Days selected: Sat (start) and Mon. Monday after start is Nov 16, which is in the next week (1 week later). With interval 2, it shouldn't occur. So Nov 16 seems wrong unless the app uses \"the week immediately following when a new weekday is added\". Hmm, hard to say. But likely a genuine bug? Not sure. This is the kind of subtle logic that the build change might've introduced.\n\nLet's be careful. Maybe the model computes schedule by \"every N weeks, on the selected weekdays, starting from start date\". The Home tab cards show upcoming occurrences. Let me save and compare Plan/Home. But before that, the \"PREVIEW\" may itself list upcoming occurrences, which should match Home. Let me check by saving and looking at Home's upcoming.\n\nActually wait — this may reveal a discrepancy between the group editor preview/summary and Home cards. The change says summary generated from same model as Home cards — perhaps the bug is that they're now consistent but wrong? Hmm.\n\nLet me reconsider: The \"PREVIEW\" section shows next few dose dates. For 2-week interval, starting Sat Nov 14, adding Mon: The recurrence \"repeat every 2 weeks\" with days {Sat, Mon}. Depending on implementation, the \"week\" anchor might be a rolling 7-day window from start date: days within each 14-day period beginning Nov 14. Period 1: Nov 14–27 includes Sat Nov 14, Mon Nov 16, Sat Nov 21? Wait Nov 21 is Sat within period 1 (Nov 14-27) - but the selected days are Sat and Mon; Nov 21 Sat would be in period 1 too. So occurrences would be Nov 14, Nov 16, Nov 21, Nov 23, Nov 28... no, then it degenerates to weekly.\n\nHmm, actually if days-of-week includes both Sat and Mon and interval 2 weeks, the natural rule: occurrence every 2 weeks on Sat and Mon = dates where weeks since epoch week divisible by 2 relative to anchor week, and weekday in {Mon, Sat}. That gives Mon Nov 9(anchor week), Sat Nov 14, then Mon Nov 23, Sat Nov 28... So Nov 16 should not appear. Preview shows Nov 16 → likely bug.\n\nWait but maybe anchor week is not Nov 9-15 but the start date is considered and Monday Nov 16 is in a different week than Monday? Let me be precise: Nov 14 2026? No, date shows Nov 14 Sat. In 2026, Nov 14 is Saturday. Week of Nov 9 (Mon) to Nov 15 (Sun). Next Mon = Nov 16. Weeks: W0 = Nov 9-15, W1 = Nov 16-22, W2 = Nov 23-29. Every 2 weeks anchored W0 → W0, W2, W4... Mondays: Nov 9 (past), Nov 23, Dec 7. Saturdays: Nov 14, Nov 28, Dec 12. So eventually preview after today: Nov 14(today), Nov 23 Mon, Nov 28 Sat. It shows Nov 16 Mon → mismatch.\n\nUnless \"repeat every 2 weeks\" anchors differently when days selected — e.g., each day-of-week first occurrence computed from start date: Monday next occurrence = Nov 16 (start date is Sat; next Monday is Nov 16), then +2 weeks = Nov 30. Saturday occurrences: Nov 14, Nov 28. So preview would be Nov 16 Mon, Nov 28 Sat, Nov 30 Mon — which is exactly what's shown? We only see two occurrences: Nov 16, Nov 28. Hmm that's consistent with per-weekday anchoring: Mon Nov 16, Sat Nov 14(today), Sat Nov 28, Mon Nov 30. But preview shows Nov 16 and Nov 28, skipping Nov 21. So the model might be per-weekday with 2-week interval anchored at each weekday's first occurrence after start. With that, Mon: Nov 16, Nov 30; Sat: Nov 14, Nov 28. Combined next 3: Nov 14, Nov 16, Nov 28. Exactly what's displayed! So it could be intended semantics.\n\nHmm, ambiguous. Hard to call bug. Maybe there's an actual inconsistency between preview and Home. Let's save with this schedule and compare Home/Plan.\n\nBut careful: changing data. It's fine, testing requires it. Let me Save and check Home upcoming and Plan summary.\n\nActually before saving, note the Plan card summary while editing is still the old \"Every week · Sat · 7:00 AM\" until save.\n\nSave now."}
