ds a new card? The EditText is the note content, so saving updates. Possibly one note per day.\n\nHmm.\n\nLet me try a different route: maybe the Journal is also accessible via Home's \"More options\" or the Journal has a \"Timeline\" within it. We have the Timeline screen.\n\nI think the Timeline screen is the one. Let's test pagination by adding enough entries. I'll add several with distinct dates including months. Let me do it efficiently.\n\nPlan: create 8 more dates: Nov 1, Nov 2, Nov 3, Nov 4, Nov 5, Nov 6, Nov 7, Nov 8. Then the ALL DATES list will have 11 entries. Scrolling may load/reorder. Observe order and duplicates.\n\nActually, maybe pagination is triggered by scroll regardless of count: the screen loads a first page (e.g., 20) and fetches next page when scrolled to the end. With 11 entries, if page size 20, no.\n\nHmm. What if page size is 10? Then 11 triggers page 2. Let's aim for 15 entries to be safe? That's a lot.\n\nMaybe I should look for evidence of page size from UI: The ALL DATES list at 3 entries is not scrollable because content fits. If the screen initially loads a fixed 10, we'd see 10 entries and no more until scroll. Let's just build to 12 and observe.\n\nLet me be efficient: add entries with today's date (default) — 4 calls each. Duplicates allowed? Let's test one duplicate now: add \"Dup1\" with default date today.\n\nNavigate: BACK from History → Plan; then Journal tab; timeline card; add."}
