{"type": "thinking", "text": "Reproduced: changing START DATE from Nov 14 to Nov 15 changed START TIME from 6:36 AM to 4:00 AM. This is a clear unexpected side effect. Let's check what happens with night owl OFF: toggle off then change date, see if start time resets to 12:00 AM. That would confirm \"start of day\" logic. But regardless, the user changed only the date and the time changed — a bug in editing groups.\n\nHowever, is it possible that the app intentionally sets Start time to \"start of logical day\" when changing date because the previous start time is no longer valid? No, start time is independent.\n\nHmm wait, maybe the start time is actually affected by the date picker because the date picker's time is... no.\n\nLet me check: after changing date, if I tap START TIME, what time does the time picker show? And can I change it back? Also check if Save produces a group with start 4:00 AM (the summary \"Since Nov 15\" only).\n\nI think this is reportable: \"Editing the group's start date resets the start time from 6:36 AM to 4:00 AM.\" Let me confirm it's persistent: Save and reopen, then check START TIME. Let's save (with date Nov 15, time 4:00). Then plan card. Then restore date Nov 14 and time 6:36 by editing? We can set time back via time picker to 6:36 and date Nov 14.\n\nActually, let's think about whether this is a genuine bug vs. designed. The \"Start time\" likely defaults to \"Now\" when creating. When you change the start date, maybe it should keep the time. The app changed it to 4:00 AM. This is likely a bug but maybe tied to \"night owl mode\": with night owl, the start time is automatically set to 4:00 AM when date changes? Hmm.\n\nLet me test with night owl OFF to see if start time becomes 12:00 AM. Toggle night owl off (element 20) then change date. If it becomes 12:00 AM, then yes, it's \"start of logical day\" logic. Let me do that."}
