{"type": "thinking", "text": "Aha! Toggling Night owl mode off changed START TIME from 4:00 AM to 12:00 AM. So the start time is being forced to the \"day boundary\" (4:00 AM with night owl, 12:00 AM without) whenever something changes? That's a significant behavior: the Start Time is not an independent field; it's derived from night owl mode? But initially (created with night owl on) start time was 6:36 AM (\"Now\"). Then changing date set it to 4:00. Then toggling night owl off set it to 12:00 AM.\n\nHmm, so \"Start time\" appears to be a logical day boundary that is auto-set when the logical day definition changes. Maybe the UI semantics: \"START TIME\" = the time the group starts. When the user changes date, the app recomputes start time to the start of the day. This could be intentional to ensure the start time isn't after the first dose? Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe when the schedule type/night owl changes, the start time is reset to the \"day start\" to keep the schedule aligned. Could be by design. But from a QA standpoint, silently changing a user-set Start time is surprising. However, the \"start time\" might not be user-set (it's \"Now\" for new groups). Let me check if tapping START TIME opens a time picker that lets you set it. If yes, it's a user-settable field, and this auto-overwrite is a bug.\n\nLet me tap START TIME (4) to see."}
