{"type": "thinking", "text": "The Start Time is user-settable (time picker with Reset). So the behavior where changing the date or night owl resets it to 12:00/4:00 AM is suspicious. But maybe the app interprets \"start time\" as the beginning of the day for the schedule. The \"Reset\" button suggests it can be reset to default (maybe 12:00/4:00).\n\nHonestly, this could be intended: \"start time\" defines the start of the schedule day and changing date resets to default. But the user could have set it to 6:36 AM (it was \"Now\" from creation). Changing date overwriting it to 4:00 AM is a data-loss bug. I'm fairly convinced this is a bug worth reporting, but it's not directly the changed \"schedule summary\" area. Still in \"editing medication groups\" area, so in scope.\n\nLet me first restore: cancel time picker, re-enable night owl? Wait we toggled night owl off (a change we may not want). We'll discard this edit anyway (cancel). Let's Cancel time picker, cancel edit, then reopen; start time should be 6:36, night owl on, date Nov 14.\n\nThen consider reporting the bug: \"Editing start date / toggling night owl silently resets Start time\".\n\nHmm, but which report would be accepted? The developer might reply \"expected: start time is derived\". Let me examine the group editor UI text: \"START\" section with START DATE and START TIME. In Add group, start time showed \"Now\". So start time = actual datetime the group begins. When you change the start date to a future date, keeping the time \"Now\" would be odd (Now = 6:36 AM on a future date). The app might reasonably snap the start time to the beginning of that day. But snapping to 4:00 AM because night owl is on seems logical: the \"logical day\" starts at 4 AM, so group starts at 4:00 AM on the selected date. Hmm! That actually seems intentionally designed: when you pick a start date, the start time defaults to the start of that logical day (midnight, or 4 AM in night owl mode). Hmm.\n\nActually wait: when we changed date from Nov 14 to Nov 15, the start time became 4:00 AM (night owl on). Then toggling night owl off changed it to 12:00 AM. That's consistent with \"start time = start of logical day\" derived from night owl. But then why is there a separate START TIME picker? Maybe it allows overriding the start time, but any change to date/night owl re-derives it. Could be intended to keep consistency. Hmm, harder to call bug.\n\nGiven uncertainty, maybe not report. Let me abandon this line.\n\nLet me cancel the time picker and discard edits to restore original group state."}
