\n\nMaybe the \"Journal timeline\" is actually the NOTES list on the Journal tab: a timeline of journal entries, newest first, older pages loaded at the bottom. That matches \"oldest pages last\" and \"entries are now paged in as the timeline scrolls\". The \"No earlier notes.\" is the end-of-list. This is likely it. The Timeline screen is a separate \"Timeline\" feature (dates), not the \"journal timeline\".\n\nThen what are the journal entries? Notes! But one per day. So the journal timeline shows notes for the last 30 days, sorted newest first, with older days' notes paged in as you scroll. To test pagination we'd need notes on multiple days. Which we can't create via UI... unless the app allows writing notes for previous days somewhere. \n\nWait, maybe the note is tied to a selected day via the \"Today Nov 14 Sat\" header — could be a date selector. It's marked disabled, but maybe tapping the date text opens a date picker? Let's try tapping exactly on \"Nov 14 Sat\" text. Earlier I tapped the container and nothing. Let me try tapping the text region (x≈730,y=855?) Actually the header row \"Today | Nov 14 Sat\" at y=855. Let me tap x=760,y=855."}
